{"type":"message","id":"29feea2d","parentId":"57bf7347","timestamp":"2026-10-19T11:20:02.080Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"chatcmpl-tool-a8be40ddf6e3b837","toolName":"bash","content":[{"type":"text","text":"=== search O7 uncharged/backoff in docs ===\n.collab/BOARD.md:1254:notes: RECORDED, NOT FIXED (owner: finish then stop): if write_atomic fails and its own temp unlink fails, the temp stays until the next boot sweep (optional best-effort drop in flag_argv before the raise); _MCP_TMP uses \\d (matches Unicode digits; [0-9]+ would be exact); note_failure labels a flag_argv write failure isolation_failed on the isolated path; T-103's secrets gate must follow the write_atomic writer at the merge. FIXED b73f875 (Claude fork, 2026-10-15): drop_mcp_config (mark_ended + boot sweep) also removes every file in the same res directory whose name fully matches write_atomic's temp shape for the config, mcp.json.<digits>.tmp, nothing else; tests: an end removes a planted temp, the boot sweep removes a temp left with no mcp.json and keeps a watched execution's, six look-alike siblings untouched; mutants 3 of 3 caught (temps kept, every \"mcp*\" removed, prefix match); test_settings_sources + test_execution 105 passed (-m \"not real_process\"); ruff clean, no CR. FOLLOW-UP CHANGES (blocking, D7 regression from 0fb5daa): write_atomic leaves mcp.json.<pid>.tmp holding the keys when its best-effort delete fails (silent) or Core dies before os.replace; drop_mcp_config (mark_ended + boot sweep) removes only mcp.json - fix: drop_mcp_config also removes mcp.json.*.tmp in the same directory, test both shapes. FIXING (Claude fork). FOLLOW-UP 0fb5daa (2026-10-15, Claude fork; reviews/T-102-438d5ca.claude.md findings 1-2): sources.flag_argv writes res/mcp.json through config.write_atomic and raises SpawnWriteFailed when it cannot, so a persistent MCP-config write failure is charged `workspace` and ends the task FAILED (was: PermissionError out of the tick, Core exit 3, then uncharged binding on restart); tests pin a stale ended/halted.json removal failure and a class-dir makedirs failure as charged workspace. Mutants 4 of 4 caught. Focused 665 passed, 2 skipped. INTEGRATION NOTE: T-103's secrets gate (D:/archeus-p20-h) names flag_argv's open() write as the MCP writer; the merge must point it at the write_atomic call. Finding 3 (LocalNode.spawn notes a SpawnWriteFailed as isolation_failed on the isolated path) not addressed, latent. CORRECTION 438d5ca: a pre-child write failure is charged. _start does its pre-child writes (class dirs, marker, stale tombstone/halt report, prompt) in one block; their OSError becomes base.SpawnWriteFailed (a SpawnFailed subclass) and the manager refuses it with the charged `workspace` stop reason (P11 note 11), so a persistent failure spends max_attempts and the task ends FAILED. A launch's own SpawnFailed stays uncharged `binding` (O7); an OSError the launch raises is still an uncharged refusal, not a crash; any non-OSError propagates. Commit message corrects c91d4f1's \"aborted the whole tick\" (it stopped the execution thread and Core). Tests: never-writable prompt -> two charged workspace attempts, task FAILED; one-off -> charged once, retry ENDED_OK; launch SpawnFailed stays binding; RuntimeError propagates, nothing refused. OPEN, not this card: a permanent Popen failure (spawn_detached returning None) still re-dispatches uncharged every tick - O7's backoff/breaker; _private_dirs/_isolated_env failures on the isolated path stay uncharged (isolation establishment, O7). REVIEW CHANGES (blocking): a pre-child spawn OSError now ends as uncharged `binding` with no retry bound - a persistent prompt-write failure produced 70 ABANDONED executions in 4 s, task still READY (max_attempts 2); before, it stopped Core and was reconciled LOST (charged). p11 note 11 limits binding to a stale plan or provider terms; owner O7 (2026-10-08) makes only isolation-establishment failures uncharged, with a backoff/breaker not yet built. Fix: charge it as `workspace` (like _workspace and the inventory failure), test a persistent failure ends FAILED, pin the refusal to OSError only (a surviving mutant). Non-blocking: kill does not survive a Core restart (T-105); POSIX tree kill is SIGTERM to the group; tests fake \"still running\"; commit message overstates. FIXING 2026-10-15 (Claude fork). DONE c91d4f1: (1) manager._orphans(live, disarmed): an orphan still running gets p['since'] on first sight and is killed through node.kill once grace_s has passed (the existing STOPPING grace, Rig 0.3 s, default 10 s - no new constant), at once when disarmed; collected by the next pass (tombstone, mcp.json dropped). (2) base.spawn: an OSError from _start (before any child) goes through the existing _refuse (tombstone + SpawnFailed), so _spawn refuses the execution with stop_reason binding and the tick continues; a post-child OSError is unchanged. test_T099_a_prompt_that_cannot_be_written now asserts the refusal, the tombstone error and the retry reaching ENDED_OK. Pre-existing, found by the T-099 review: _orphans collects only processes that already exited and kills nothing, so a halted process that never exits keeps its config and is never killed by Core. Proposed; Claude takes it after T-101 under the owner rule of 2026-10-15 unless the owner objects (bounded grace value to be named on the card at claim).\n.collab/BOARD.md:1293:refs: reviews/T-102-c91d4f1.claude.md (a permanent Popen failure loops: 63 executions in 4 s, pre-existing); owner decision O7 2026-10-08 (isolation-establishment failures uncharged, with a backoff and breaker).\n.collab/BOARD.md:1397:refs: T-106; owner decision O7 2026-10-08 (isolation-establishment failures uncharged, with a backoff and breaker); reviews/T-102-c91d4f1.claude.md (63 executions in 4 s on a permanent Popen failure); docs/architecture/ (find O7 and every \"backoff\"/\"breaker\" for dispatch or spawn).\n.collab/QWEN-CARD-T-110.md:5:refs: T-106; owner decision O7 2026-10-08 (isolation-establishment failures uncharged, with a backoff and breaker); reviews/T-102-c91d4f1.claude.md (63 executions in 4 s on a permanent Popen failure); docs/architecture/ (find O7 and every \"backoff\"/\"breaker\" for dispatch or spawn).\n.collab/reviews/T-102-438d5ca.claude.md:5:The blocking finding is fixed. A write that Core makes before any child exists, inside `_start`'s block (class directories, marker, stale `ended`/`halted.json` removal, prompt), now raises `base.SpawnWriteFailed`. `_spawn` refuses that with the charged `workspace` stop reason (manager.py:323-330). A persistent failure spends `max_attempts` and the task ends FAILED: the test counts exactly two executions, both `('ABANDONED', 'workspace', True)`, with max_attempts 2. A launch's own SpawnFailed stays uncharged `binding`, as O7 decides. Its OSError fallback at base.py:330 is still a refusal and not a crash. A non-OSError raised before any child now propagates, which was the surviving mutant M6 in the last review. The charged class matches p11 note 11 (\"`binding` again means only a stale plan binding (��7) or provider terms\"; a workspace that cannot be made is charged). It also matches the O7 decision of 2026-10-08 (PV20-S1-GATE ��7), where only an isolation-establishment failure is uncharged. None of the newly charged writes is isolation establishment. `_private_dirs`, `_isolated_env` and `isolation.launch` all sit outside the block and stay `binding`, and the class-1..3 grants are planned in establish, not in the makedirs. The commit message now corrects c91d4f1's \"aborted the whole tick\" wording.\n.collab/reviews/T-102-c91d4f1.claude.md:10:   Canonical conflict: p11-design-gate note 11 (D9) says \"`binding` again means only a stale plan binding (��7) or provider terms\". It made a workspace that cannot be made a **charged** `stop_reason='workspace'`, because the uncharged version looped 395 times in one run. The manager states the same rule at manager.py:288-293 for the settings inventory: \"an uncharged end re-dispatches the task, so a failure that persists would start a new execution on every tick, forever\". `_workspace` already charges an OSError from `os.makedirs(ExecPaths(e.id).work)`, which is the same tree base.spawn creates. The owner's O7 decision (PV20-S1-GATE ��7, 2026-10-08) makes only an *isolation-establishment* SpawnFailed uncharged, and even that only \"under a bounded backoff policy\" with a breaker. No such mechanism exists yet. A prompt or marker write failure is not isolation establishment.\n=== .collab status files ===\nBOARD.md\nQWEN-CARD-T-110.md\nQWEN-CARD-T-114.md\nQWEN-DONE-T-114.md\nQWEN-NEXT.md\nREADME.md\nSTATUS-2026-10-12.md\nSTATUS-2026-10-13.md\nSTATUS-2026-10-14.md\nT-004-evidence.md\nT-010-creator-access.md\nT-015-gap-b-matrix.md\nT-016-private-workspace-plan.md\nT-017-private-config-plan.md\nT-018-arrival-policy.md\nT-021-isolation-decision-contract.md\nT-025-limit-report-authority.md\nT-030-seed-import-contract.md\nT-031-isolated-environment-contract.md\nT-034-staged-runtime-contract.md\nT-035-isolated-provenance-contract.md\nT-037-lost-isolation-record-contract.md\nT-041-verification-guard-contract.md\nT-043-isolated-facts-contract.md\nT-045-regression-report.md\nT-046-core-git-store-contract.md\nT-047-regression-report.md\nT-049-seed-contract.md\nT-050-provider-broker-contract.md\nT-051-import-contract.md\nT-052-creator-authority-decision.md\nT-053-origin-transport-contract.md\nT-054-confined-verifier-contract.md\nT-071-storage-namespace-options.md\nT-072-integration-inventory.md\nT-072-prereview.md\nT-072-regression-report.md\nT-075-k03-flake.md\nT-077-long-home.md\nT-079-worktree-layout.md\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1792408802080}}
