{"type":"message","id":"7b05be0a","parentId":"6912fc09","timestamp":"2026-10-19T11:25:04.476Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"chatcmpl-tool-b1add2f5b70ff038","toolName":"bash","content":[{"type":"text","text":"1560:     def __init__(self, authority, request):\n1561:         self.authority = authority\n1562:         self.request = request\n1563:         self.execution_id = request.execution_id\n1564: \n1565:     # �"?�"? the mechanism (��3.4) �"?�"?\n1566: \n1567:     def launch(self, argv, *, cwd, env, paths):\n1568:         \"\"\"Create the process inside the execution identity and inside its Core-held\n1569:         Job, with Core's own handles for stdin, stdout and stderr (��3.3: \"the prompt\n1570:         and the stream reach the process as Core-opened handles\"). Returns\n1571:         `(child, None)` like `proc.spawn_detached`; every failure raises\n1572:         `base.SpawnFailed` after the deterministic state is recorded.\"\"\"\n1573:         api = self.authority.boundary\n1574:         try:\n1575:             rec = self.authority.establish(self.request, paths)\n1576:         except IsolationUnavailable as err:\n1577:             raise base.SpawnFailed('isolation: %s%s' % (err.reason,\n1578:                                                         ' (%s)' % err.detail if err.detail else ''))\n1579:         handles = []\n1580:         try:\n1581:             handles.append(api.open_inherited(paths.prompt, 'read'))\n1582:             handles.append(api.open_inherited(paths.stream, 'append'))\n1583:             child = api.launch(list(argv), cwd=cwd, env=env, profile=rec.profile,\n1584:                                job=self.authority.held_job(rec.execution_id),\n1585:                                stdin=handles[0], stdout=handles[1])\n1586:             # held before anything else can fail, so the end path waits on this process\n1587:             # by its own handle and never by a PID that may name another one by then\n1588:             self.authority._live[rec.execution_id] = child\n1589:             rec.pid, rec.create_time = child.pid, base_create_time(child.pid)\n1590:             self.authority._save(rec)\n1591:             return child, None\n1592:         except Exception as err:                       # nothing half-started survives\n1593:             # a process created and then not confined or not resumed was terminated by\n1594:             # the boundary, and is held here like a launched one, so the end path waits\n1595:             # on it by its own handle; the record never names it launched\n1596:             failed = getattr(err, 'child', None)\n1597:             if failed is not None:\n1598:                 self.authority._live[rec.execution_id] = failed\n1599:             if isinstance(err, IsolationUnavailable):\n1600:                 raise base.SpawnFailed('isolation: %s%s' % (\n1601:                     err.reason, ' (%s)' % err.detail if err.detail else ''))\n1602:             raise base.SpawnFailed('isolation: launch_failed (%s)' % err)\n1603:         finally:\n1604:             for h in handles:\n1605:                 try:\n1606:                     api.close_handle(h)\n1607:                 except Exception:\n1608:                     pass\n1609: \n1610:     # what `base.spawn` and the registry read afterwards\n1611:     def facts(self):\n1612:         rec = self.authority.record(self.execution_id)\n1613:         if rec is None:\n1614:             return {}\n1615:         return {'isolated': True, 'ac_profile': rec.profile, 'ac_sid': rec.sid,\n1616:                 'capabilities': list(rec.capabilities), 'isolation_state': rec.state,\n1617:                 'job': 'core-held-unnamed-kill-on-close'}\n1618: \n1619: \n1620: def base_create_time(pid):\n1621:     from claude_sessions import proc\n1622:     return proc.process_create_time(pid)\n1623: \n1624: \n1625: # �"?�"? the OS boundary �"?�"?�"?�"?�"?�"?�"?�"?�"?�"?�"?�"?�"?�"?�"?�"?�"?�"?�"?�"?�"?�"?�"?�"?�"?�"?�"?�"?�"?�"?�"?�"?�"?�"?�"?�"?�"?�"?�"?�"?�"?�"?�"?�"?�"?�"?�"?�"?�"?�"?�"?�"?�"?�"?�"?�"?�"?�"?\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1792409104476}}
{"type":"message","id":"a48f7b39","parentId":"7b05be0a","timestamp":"2026-10-19T11:25:12.189Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I now have all the pieces for the analysis. Let me also check whether there is any existing \"backoff\" mechanism in Core dispatch (search for retry/backoff in manager/engine, and `since`-based gating) �?" to state whether the design names a backoff mechanism anywhere. And check state-machines.md ��9 for breaker thresholds referenced by p11 D23.\n\nAlso check the T-106 card reference to understand what the note should feed �?" but I shouldn't read BOARD.md. The card says \"Feeds T-106\". I don't need T-106 details; the accept criteria are explicit.\n\nLet me check state-machines ��9 (breaker thresholds) as the canonical naming of thresholds, and whether any canonical doc names a location/threshold/window/reset/visibility for an O7 breaker.\n","thinkingSignature":"reasoning"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"chatcmpl-tool-b37811647766482f","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"cd /d/Claude/docs/architecture && echo \"=== state-machines ��9 ===\"; grep -n \"## 9\\|### 9\\|��9\" state-machines.md | head; echo \"---\"; awk '/^## 9/,/^## 10/' state-machines.md | head -40"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"spark","model":"qwen3.8-flash-next","usage":{"input":1149,"output":271,"cacheRead":58240,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":175,"totalTokens":59660,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1792409104478,"responseId":"chatcmpl-96b5ce0981b2cee1","rawStopReason":"tool_calls"}}
{"type":"message","id":"ed137094","parentId":"a48f7b39","timestamp":"2026-10-19T11:25:12.338Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"chatcmpl-tool-b37811647766482f","toolName":"bash","content":[{"type":"text","text":"=== state-machines ��9 ===\n317:- *As built (P10, p10-design-gate ��9):* `no_eligible_resource` also blocks the mission with the\n579:## 9. Account health (resource availability + circuit breaker)\n---\n## 9. Account health (resource availability + circuit breaker)\n\n```mermaid\nstateDiagram-v2\n    [*] --> UNVERIFIED\n    UNVERIFIED --> AVAILABLE: auth_ok\n    UNVERIFIED --> UNAUTHENTICATED: auth_failed\n    AVAILABLE --> CONSTRAINED: near_ceiling\n    CONSTRAINED --> AVAILABLE: usage_dropped\n    AVAILABLE --> LIMITED: window_exhausted\n    CONSTRAINED --> LIMITED: window_exhausted\n    LIMITED --> AVAILABLE: reset_time_passed\n    AVAILABLE --> DEGRADED: error_storm\n    CONSTRAINED --> DEGRADED: error_storm\n    DEGRADED --> AVAILABLE: probe_ok\n    DEGRADED --> OPEN: errors_persist\n    OPEN --> DEGRADED: cooldown_elapsed\n    AVAILABLE --> UNAUTHENTICATED: auth_failed\n    UNAUTHENTICATED --> UNVERIFIED: relogin\n    AVAILABLE --> DISABLED: user_disables\n    DISABLED --> UNVERIFIED: user_enables\n```\n\n- `near_ceiling`: observed utilisation �%� `ceiling(account, task) �^' 5`, i.e.\n  `allocation_pct �^' reserve_pct �^' brain_reserve_pct �^' 5` (router ��4).\n- `window_exhausted`: provider says so (`quota.is_limit_error` / `is_window_limit` on a failure,\n  or usage �%� 100%). `limited_until = resets_at`.\n- DEGRADED/OPEN is a circuit breaker adapted from Munder Difflin's `breaker.ts`: move **at most\n  one level per beat** (beat = 60 s), de-escalate on a successful probe. OPEN accounts are never\n  routed to; DEGRADED accounts only receive work when no AVAILABLE candidate exists and policy\n  permits fallback.\n- The machine lives on Account; Harness has a simpler AVAILABLE/MISSING/MISCONFIGURED state set\n  by discovery.\n- *As built (P10):* only `auth_ok` / `auth_failed` (the adapter's probe, made before the\n  registering command) and `user_disables` / `user_enables` are fired. `near_ceiling`,\n  `window_exhausted` and `reset_time_passed` are computed by the router from each decision's own\n  snapshot (so a decision replays); the limit-error and breaker moves come with execution\n  failures in P11 (p10-design-gate ��21.1).\n\n---\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1792409112338}}
{"type":"message","id":"4c7357b1","parentId":"ed137094","timestamp":"2026-10-19T11:25:19.385Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now I have all canonical facts. Let me also check p20-design-gate line 1260 context (the O7 options) and line 1420-1430, and 2770 (the O7 deferred row). Also p11-design-gate 1015-1035 for the O7 statement.\n","thinkingSignature":"reasoning"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"chatcmpl-tool-9e2d947289f660b3","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"cd /d/Claude/docs/architecture && echo \"=== p20 1255-1270 ===\"; awk 'NR>=1243 && NR<=1270 {printf \"%d: %s\\n\", NR, $0}' p20-design-gate.md; echo \"=== p20 1415-1432 ===\"; awk 'NR>=1415 && NR<=1432 {printf \"%d: %s\\n\", NR, $0}' p20-design-gate.md; echo \"=== p20 2765-2775 ===\"; awk 'NR>=2765 && NR<=2775 {printf \"%d: %s\\n\", NR, $0}' p20-design-gate.md"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"spark","model":"qwen3.8-flash-next","usage":{"input":2023,"output":281,"cacheRead":58240,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":80,"totalTokens":60544,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1792409112341,"responseId":"chatcmpl-9d70c261af517d4d","rawStopReason":"tool_calls"}}
{"type":"message","id":"10f089ec","parentId":"4c7357b1","timestamp":"2026-10-19T11:25:19.522Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"chatcmpl-tool-9e2d947289f660b3","toolName":"bash","content":[{"type":"text","text":"=== p20 1255-1270 ===\n1243:     - The inventory is part of that preparation: it is taken before the process exists, and\n1244:       nothing spawns without it.\n1245:     - The execution's own reason names the real cause (\"the settings sources could not be\n1246:       inventoried: <error type>\"). Only the stop reason's fixed copy (\"its workspace could not\n1247:       be made\") is approximate.\n1248:     - A dedicated stop reason would be a domain addition. It is available if the user wants it,\n1249:       and not needed for correctness.\n1250: 64. **Review: P11's `SpawnFailed` re-dispatches forever (item 48). A decision is required:\n1251:     O7, OPEN.**\n1252:     - `manager.py` ends a spawn the node could not make with `stop_reason='binding'`, which is\n1253:       uncharged. P11 note 11 states that \"`binding` again means only a stale plan binding (��7) or\n1254:       provider terms\".\n1255:     - So the present behaviour contradicts P11's own definition, and it loops: 40 executions in\n1256:       40 ticks, measured in slice E.\n1257:     - It is not acceptable under the existing gate, and the fix is not implied. A missing binary\n1258:       is not plainly the task's own failure, which is what charging means. The options are:\n1259:       - a charged reason: the task fails after `max_attempts`;\n1260:       - an uncharged reason with a backoff or a harness breaker;\n1261:       - routing away from a harness that cannot spawn.\n1262:     - It is P11's code, outside slice E's authority. Nothing was changed.\n1263: 65. **The secrets limitation, restated for slice I.** `run/exec/<id>/mcp.json` holds the\n1264:     **full** definitions of the opted-in MCP servers (command, arguments, URL, environment), so\n1265:     it may contain tokens.\n1266:     - It is written only when a server is opted in. It never enters the inventory, which records\n1267:       names only (E11, I08).\n1268:     - It belongs to **slice I's secrets review (D7)**: ��14.B lists it there. It was not\n1269:       redesigned in E.\n1270:     - *Under PV-20 (ADR-0053 ��7 A2; not implemented):* **no MCP opt-in is admitted to an isolated\n=== p20 1415-1432 ===\n1415: 71. **O6, recorded and not changed.** With no source opted in, an execution receives **no\n1416:     CLAUDE.md at all**, including the project's CLAUDE.md that Archeus itself maintains (V3e).\n1417:     - Restoring the project's CLAUDE.md today requires opting in the project's whole `project`\n1418:       source, which also brings that source's hooks, permission rules and skills.\n1419:     - D6 is not changed here. Changing the default would be a separate design decision.\n1420: 72. **O7, deferred to P11.** P11 is not modified.\n1421:     - **Recorded for P11's follow-up:**\n1422:       - a process that cannot be started (`SpawnFailed`) ends its execution with\n1423:         `stop_reason='binding'`;\n1424:       - `binding` is uncharged, so no attempt is spent;\n1425:       - the task is therefore re-dispatched every tick, indefinitely (40 executions in 40 ticks,\n1426:         measured in slice E);\n1427:       - P11 note 11 defines `binding` as a stale plan binding or provider terms only.\n1428:     - The choice between charging, a backoff or breaker, and routing away from the harness is\n1429:       not made in P20.\n1430: 73. **Tests after the closeout.**\n1431:     - Focused, on the closeout tree:\n1432:       - slice E's unit (E01�?"E25, 37), integration (I01�?"I10, H01�?"H02), G6, slice E's E2E,\n=== p20 2765-2775 ===\n2765: | O1 | Re-arm re-asks the plan gate for missions blocked only by the e-stop? (they stay BLOCKED today; P9's rule) | nothing in P20's slices; V2's stop-band copy (��14.F) |\n2766: | O2 | Does Pause all (strip, Work) get F7's post-action lin